00:21:27,860 --> 00:21:31,460
怎么才能在半天时间里
榨出相当于一辈子的磨损？
How were we going to
give them a lifetime's
use in half a day?

390
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:38,020
简单。我们要开着它们去跑出租，
就在周五的夜晚，
Easy. We're going to
take them minicabbing,
on a Friday night

391
00:21:38,060 --> 00:21:39,340
在伦敦南部。
in south London.

392
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:43,220
我们的夜班
从下午四点开始，
Our shift starts at
4:00 in the afternoon,

393
00:21:43,260 --> 00:21:45,900
但要一路连轴转到
打架斗殴啃烤肉的高峰期——
but it goes all the way
through to the fighting
and kebabs hour

394
00:21:45,940 --> 00:21:48,300
也就是凌晨一点。
of 1:00 in the morning.

395
00:21:48,340 --> 00:21:51,340
那么，来看看我们要连开九个小时的
这几辆出租车吧。
So, let's have a look at the
minicabs that we'll be driving
for nine hours.

396
00:21:53,460 --> 00:21:56,820
我先从这辆
雷诺风景（Scenic）开始。
I'm going to start with
the Renault Scenic.

397
00:21:56,860 --> 00:21:58,860
它有五个座位，配置非常丰富，
It's got five seats,
it's very well-equipped,

398
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:01,940
但售价高达18500英镑，
but it costs £18,500.

399
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:05,220
比同级的雷诺两厢掀背车贵了两千镑。
two grand more than the
equivalent Renault hatchback.

400
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:10,540
这车里到处都是
储物暗格。有些挺显眼的，
There are loads of
cubbyholes in here.
Some of them quite obvious,

401
00:22:10,580 --> 00:22:13,540
比如这个，
还有些藏得没那么显眼的，
such as this one,
and some not so obvious,

402
00:22:13,580 --> 00:22:15,260
比如……
such as...

403
00:22:16,620 --> 00:22:18,500
……这一个。
...this one.

404
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:22,580
中央扶手箱
还能前后滑动，
And the centre console
can be made to slide
backwards and forwards,

405
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:26,620
这样你就能牺牲后排腿部空间
来换几个杯架。
so you can trade rear legroom
for cup holders.

406
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:28,100
还没完呢。
And there's more.

407
00:22:28,140 --> 00:22:30,460
后排有三个
独立座椅。
There are three
individual rear seats.

408
00:22:30,500 --> 00:22:34,580
全都能滑动、能折叠，
甚至还能直接彻底拆下来，
They all slide, they all fold,
or they can all be removed
completely,

409
00:22:34,620 --> 00:22:37,220
方便你兼职客串
带随车司机的货运小面包。
so that you can
moonlight as a van
with a helpful driver.

410
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:43,660
哈蒙德：
而这辆是福特给出的答案。
HAMMOND:
And this is Ford's version.

411
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:47,380
名叫C-Max，
基于下一代福克斯打造，
It's called the C-Max.
It's based on the next Focus

412
00:22:47,420 --> 00:22:53,660
它同样有五个座位，
以及高达16,500英镑的
肉疼售价。
and it, too, has got
five seats and a
hefty price tag of £16,500.

413
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:56,140
这车个头挺高，
It's a tall car,

414
00:22:56,180 --> 00:22:57,980
大概是给大高个儿开的吧。
presumably for tall people.

415
00:22:58,020 --> 00:23:00,300
核载五人，但如果
你们只有四个人，
It seats five, but if
there's only four of you,

416
00:23:00,340 --> 00:23:03,340
那后排这两位乘客可就有福了，
then the rear two seat
passengers have got a treat

417
00:23:03,380 --> 00:23:05,060
因为你可以把中间那个小座椅往前翻，
because you can roll
that little seat forwards,

418
00:23:05,100 --> 00:23:06,980
甚至能直接给它整拆出来。
actually take that
out completely.

419
00:23:07,020 --> 00:23:11,260
然后两侧座椅往后滑、向中间靠拢，
相当精妙的设计。
Then the outer two slide
backwards and together,
which is clever.

420
00:23:11,300 --> 00:23:14,060
再看前排，
这里有个中央扶手箱。
Then at the front,
there's the centre console.

421
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:15,460
虽然不能前后滑动什么的，
It doesn't move
around or anything,

422
00:23:15,500 --> 00:23:16,900
但它跟个机关解谜盒似的。
but it's like one
of those puzzles.

423
00:23:16,940 --> 00:23:19,500
掀开顶盖，有这么点储物格，
Open the top, and there's
a bit of storage space,

424
00:23:19,540 --> 00:23:22,180
再往下一掀，瞧瞧，大得很！
And then you open it up again,
and look, there's loads!

425
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:23,820
装进去睡一觉都行。
That's somewhere to sleep.

426
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:25,580
最后，还有这个。
And then finally, this.

427
00:23:25,620 --> 00:23:29,100
一个类似公交车司机用的
凸面后视镜，
A kind of convex
bus driver's mirror

428
00:23:29,140 --> 00:23:31,620
方便你随时盯着后排熊孩子在干嘛。
so you can see what the
kids are doing in the back.

429
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:35,180
我觉得在我今晚的
网约出租车生涯里，这玩意儿肯定用得上。
I reckon that might
come in handy in my
night of minicabbing.

430
00:23:40,420 --> 00:23:42,300
哈蒙德：
今晚天气够冷的，
HAMMOND:
It's going to be a cold night,

431
00:23:42,340 --> 00:23:44,220
估计生意会很火爆。
which should be
good for business.

432
00:23:46,780 --> 00:23:50,700
车队调度中心估计
今晚能接大概150单。
The minicab office
reckons it's going
to get about 150 calls.

433
00:23:50,740 --> 00:23:52,140
[电话铃响]
[PHONE RINGING]

434
00:23:52,180 --> 00:23:53,700
您好，出租车调度。
Hello, car service.

435
00:23:53,740 --> 00:23:55,820
468号，你要去哪儿？
468, where are you going?

436
00:23:55,860 --> 00:23:59,100
哈蒙德：所以在接单上岗前，咱得先加点油。
按黑车司机的规矩来。
HAMMOND: So, before we
clock on, we'd better fill up.
Minicab style.

437
00:24:01,660 --> 00:24:03,140
这点儿应该够了。
That should do it.

438
00:24:04,020 --> 00:24:06,660
去温布尔登，
帕默斯顿路。
And Wimbledon,
Palmerston Road.

439
00:24:06,700 --> 00:24:08,700
[嘈杂的人声]
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

440
00:24:08,740 --> 00:24:11,020
要不要我跟你们说说这事儿最让我震惊的是什么？
Shall I tell you what really
amazes me about this?

441
00:24:11,060 --> 00:24:13,580
我去参加考核的时候，
得填一大堆表格，
When I went for the test,
I had to fill in a huge form

442
00:24:13,620 --> 00:24:16,660
上面要证明我没杀过人，
不是精神病……
that said I hadn't
murdered anybody,
I wasn't psychotic...

443
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:18,340
-而且你会开车。
-……我会开车。
-And you could drive a car.
-... I could drive a car.

444
00:24:18,380 --> 00:24:20,380
不会去推翻英国政府，
I wasn't gonna overthrow
the British government,

445
00:24:20,420 --> 00:24:24,900
然后我还去体检了。
但在发证的整个过程里，
压根就没人
and then I had a medical.
At no point did anybody,
issuing this,

446
00:24:24,940 --> 00:24:27,460
-问过我分不分得清东西南北！
-[电话铃响]
-ask me if I had
a sense of direction!
-[PHONE RINGING]

447
00:24:27,500 --> 00:24:31,060
梅：行了，很快就能见分晓了，
因为活儿来了。
MAY: Well, we'll soon
find out, 'cause here we go.

448
00:24:32,740 --> 00:24:34,700
-调度员：UK-98，
准备好了吗？
-是我。
-DISPATCHER: UK-98,
are you ready?
-This is me.

449
00:24:34,740 --> 00:24:39,740
调度员：
你的单子是温布尔登公园路333号，
玛丽叫的车，两位。
DISPATCHER:
You want 333 Wimbledon
Park Road, two for Mary.

450
00:24:39,780 --> 00:24:42,740
收到，多谢。
Roger. Thank you.

451
00:24:42,780 --> 00:24:46,700
调度员：UK-99，你要去
莫顿路转角处的雷普林汉姆路。
DISPATCHER: UK-99, you want
Replingham Road off
Merton Road.

452
00:24:46,740 --> 00:24:48,500
雷普林汉姆路？
Replingham Road?

453
00:24:50,060 --> 00:24:53,580
好嘞，走起。出车拉活喽。
Okay, here we go. Minicabbing.

454
00:24:53,620 --> 00:24:54,820
[深吸一口气]
[INHALING DEEPLY]

455
00:24:56,980 --> 00:25:00,540
梅：和哈蒙德的出租车不同，
我这辆雷诺
其实自带卫星导航，
MAY: Unlike Hammond's
minicab, my Renault
actually has sat nav,

456
00:25:00,580 --> 00:25:03,020
但要是用了就算作弊，
因为第一：
but I'd be
cheating if I used it,
because A:

457
00:25:03,060 --> 00:25:06,700
这是要花一千英镑的选配，
哪辆出租车会装；
第二：
it's a £1,000 option and
no minicab would have it,
and B:

458
00:25:06,740 --> 00:25:10,380
用了就意味着
我真知道自己该往哪开了。
and it would mean I actually
knew where I was going.

459
00:25:10,420 --> 00:25:13,540
所以退而求其次，我弄了个
塑料黏贴式指南针，
So instead, I've got
a plastic stick-on compass,

460
00:25:13,580 --> 00:25:16,300
当然，还有那本
靠谱的老式A-Z地图册，
and of course,
the trusty old A-Z,

461
00:25:17,060 --> 00:25:18,460
不过现在掉页掉得更像B-Z了。
which is now more like a B-Z.

462
00:25:20,180 --> 00:25:24,660
我把暖气开开了，
简直热得跟个
火炉似的。
I've got the heaters on,
really quite incredibly
furnace warm.

463
00:25:24,700 --> 00:25:26,060
先左拐，再右拐。
Left, then right.

464
00:25:26,100 --> 00:25:28,420
-我觉得这挺关键的。
-见鬼！
-I think that's important.
-Cack!

465
00:25:28,460 --> 00:25:31,100
梅：彻底走反了。
MAY: Right the other way.

466
00:25:31,140 --> 00:25:35,620
哈蒙德：除了强劲的
暖风，这台C-Max还配了
一套绝妙的音响。
HAMMOND: Besides powerful
heaters, the C-Max also has
a cracking stereo.

467
00:25:35,660 --> 00:25:37,820
足够搜出那个电台——
Good enough to
find that station

468
00:25:37,860 --> 00:25:40,380
那个似乎只有在出租车里
才能听到的电台。
that only seems
available in minicabs.

469
00:25:40,420 --> 00:25:45,420
[柔和爵士乐响起]
来喽，这就对了。
噢，舒服。
[SMOOTH JAZZ PLAYING]
There we go, there we go.
Oh, yeah.

470
00:25:49,180 --> 00:25:50,780
好了，左边这儿应该就是了。
Right, this should
be it on the left.

471
00:25:55,500 --> 00:25:58,820
不得不说，
这里头是有那么点压抑，
It is, I've got to say,
a bit gloomy in here,

472
00:25:58,860 --> 00:26:00,500
但空间那是真大。
but there's loads of space.

473
00:26:00,540 --> 00:26:02,340
要是调度中心现在来个电话，
If I got a call from control
right now,

474
00:26:02,380 --> 00:26:04,540
说教皇要从夜店打车走人，
saying the Pope needed
picking up from a nightclub,

475
00:26:05,300 --> 00:26:07,180
毫无压力，直接塞进来。
no worries. Straight in here.

476
00:26:09,580 --> 00:26:11,900
玛丽？
Mary?

477
00:26:11,940 --> 00:26:15,140
哈蒙德：老实说，
由我来测头部空间
可能不太合适。
HAMMOND: In truth,
I'm probably not the
one to test for headroom.

478
00:26:15,180 --> 00:26:19,220
-但我这第一位客人，
那可就完全是另一回事了。
-我是来接您的车。
-But my first customer,
that was a different matter.
-I'm your cab.

479
00:26:20,380 --> 00:26:22,300
-话说，您可真够高的。
-确实。
-Now, you're really tall.
-I am.

480
00:26:22,340 --> 00:26:24,460
-所以……
-想知道我多高好做数据统计吗？
-So...
-Do you wanna know
how tall I am, for stats?

481
00:26:24,500 --> 00:26:26,820
-你多高？老实说。
-6英尺5寸半（约1米97）。
-How tall are you? Go on.
-6'5" and a half.

482
00:26:26,860 --> 00:26:29,140
我对这位乘客有种
不太妙的预感。
I've got a slightly bad
feeling about this one.

483
00:26:29,740 --> 00:26:31,700
里面坐得下你吗？
And have you got room?

484
00:26:31,740 --> 00:26:33,540
呃，坐这种车
我的头部空间向来是个大问题。
Well, I have a problem
with head room in a
lot of these cars.

485
00:26:33,580 --> 00:26:35,660
你看，坐这里确实有点
顶脑袋，不过嘛……
And look, there's a little
bit of a headroom problem
here, but you know.

486
00:26:35,700 --> 00:26:37,540
也还算凑合吧。
It's not bad.

487
00:26:37,580 --> 00:26:40,860
哈蒙德：当法医有什么福利待遇吗？
HAMMOND: Are there any
perks to being a pathologist?

488
00:26:40,900 --> 00:26:44,420
梅：当我终于接到第一单客人时，
她刚好是个击剑运动员，
MAY: When I did
find my first fare,
she happened to be a fencer,

489
00:26:44,460 --> 00:26:47,140
还带了一大包
又长又漂亮的佩剑。
with a bag of
nice, long swords.

490
00:26:47,180 --> 00:26:49,740
对雷诺风景来说，
这倒是个绝佳的考验。
An ideal test, then,
for the Scenic.

491
00:26:49,780 --> 00:26:51,580
它的后备厢
能塞得下吗？
Would its boot
swallow them up?

492
00:26:52,220 --> 00:26:53,660
-不能。
-完全塞不下。
-No.
-No.

493
00:26:53,700 --> 00:26:55,100
-谢啦，马克。
-很高兴认识你。
-Cheers, Mark.
-Nice to meet you.

494
00:26:57,900 --> 00:27:01,220
我的第一单客人。
My first fare.

495
00:27:01,260 --> 00:27:04,660
我敢打赌詹姆斯肯定会帮客人拎包上车。
“让我来为您效劳吧。”
Bet you James carries
their bags to the car.
"Let me do that for you."

496
00:27:04,700 --> 00:27:06,740
-这包挺沉的啊。
-额，确实有点沉。
-These are heavy.
-Um, a little bit, yes.

497
00:27:06,780 --> 00:27:10,260
说实话，他平时对谁都是这副老派德行。
他肯定还会给人开车门。
He does that for
people, anyway, to be honest.
And he'll open the door.

498
00:27:10,300 --> 00:27:15,300
比起拉活的出租车司机，
他更像个专属私人司机。
He's more your chauffeur
than your minicabber.

499
00:27:15,340 --> 00:27:18,780
梅：遗憾的是，那些剑
只能堆到前排座上了。
MAY: The swords, sadly,
had to go in the front.

500
00:27:18,820 --> 00:27:21,260
好了，实在不好意思啊。
我业务还不太熟练。
Right, sorry about all that.
I'm a bit new to this.

501
00:27:21,300 --> 00:27:24,220
我不是正经开出租的。
我其实是做电视节目的。
I'm not a real minicabber.
I'm on TV, really.

502
00:27:24,260 --> 00:27:25,460
这可不是我的正经工作。
This isn't my real job.

503
00:27:27,540 --> 00:27:30,220
-去雷普灵汉姆路，好的。
-谢谢。
-Replingham Road. Okay.
-Thank you.

504
00:27:30,260 --> 00:27:32,380
这是台雷诺风景，
It's a Renault Scenic,

505
00:27:32,420 --> 00:27:35,100
座椅布局非常灵活多变。
你会发现只要拉住那个小把手，
with very versatile seating.
You'll find if you grab
hold of the little lever

506
00:27:35,140 --> 00:27:37,820
就可以前后滑动调节。
you can slide it
backwards and forwards.

507
00:27:37,860 --> 00:27:41,460
-这个吗？
-不不不，
那是前排扶手。
-This?
-No, no, no.
That's the front armrest.

508
00:27:41,500 --> 00:27:44,140
雷普灵汉姆……
我刚才就在那儿啊！
Replingham...
I was just there!

509
00:27:45,140 --> 00:27:47,300
我才刚刚掉完头！
I've just turned 'round!

510
00:27:49,900 --> 00:27:52,180
-噢，太酷了！
-这很酷吗？
-Oh, cool!
-Is that cool?

511
00:27:52,220 --> 00:27:56,300
-我只是稍微有点担心……
-对，你甚至可以把它铺成
一张大床之类的。
-I'm just slightly worried...
-Yeah. You could turn it into
a big bed or something.

512
00:27:56,340 --> 00:27:58,900
-【门铃声】
-天呐，
要是他们全喝得烂醉怎么办？
-[DOORBELL BUZZING]
-Oh, God.
What if they're all drunk?

513
00:27:58,940 --> 00:28:03,660
所以，拍这些是为了测试
你能不能胜任当主持人吗？
So, are you being recorded
so they can test if you would
be good as a presenter?

514
00:28:03,700 --> 00:28:05,740
-不不，老子本来就是主持人好吗！
有你这么说话的吗？
-噢……
-No, no. I am a presenter.
Do you mind?
-Oh...

515
00:28:05,780 --> 00:28:07,260
-对不起，不好意思。
-这根本不是我的主业。
-Sorry, sorry.
-This isn't my real job.

516
00:28:07,300 --> 00:28:10,540
别碰老子的收音机，
小心我跟你急。
Don't turn on me radio.
Or I'll be pissed off.

517
00:28:10,580 --> 00:28:13,060
哈蒙德：终于拉到一整车人了。
HAMMOND: At last,
a car full of people.

518
00:28:13,100 --> 00:28:16,580
里面还有两个
五大三粗、橄榄球手模样的壮汉。
Including a couple of
burly rugby player types.

519
00:28:16,620 --> 00:28:19,460
-女士：呃，噢，好的。
-我们去哪儿？
-WOMAN: Um, oh, right.
-Where are we going?

520
00:28:19,500 --> 00:28:22,260
